# OpenVPN Automation Pipeline

Project: `hyperexponential/infrastructure/tools/openvpn-automation`  
Project ID: `74930740`  
Pipelines UI: https://gitlab.com/hyperexponential/infrastructure/tools/openvpn-automation/-/pipelines  
Tool: `glab` (requires `glab auth login` if token expired)

Companion skill: **`jira-my-tickets`** (query 5 + VPN verify checklist) for ticket intake.

Do **not** use old inputs (`USER_EMAIL`, `ENV`, `ENV_TYPE`). Current `main` uses the inputs below.

## Inputs (current `main`)

| Input | Type | Default | Notes |
|-------|------|---------|-------|
| `ACTION` | string | `""` | Required. `create`, `delete`, `get`, `audit`, `offboarding`, `restart`, `renew-server-cert` |
| `ENVS` | array | `[]` | e.g. `dev`, `hx`. For `audit`, empty = discover all OpenVPN envs |
| `USER_EMAILS` | array | `[]` | Fully-qualified emails only; used as OpenVPN CN end-to-end |
| `RESTART_SERVERS` | boolean | `true` | When `false`, no restart jobs |

### Action behaviour

- **`create` / `delete` / `get`** — act on `USER_EMAILS` (+ usually `ENVS`)
- **`audit` / `restart` / `renew-server-cert`** — act on `ENVS`, ignore `USER_EMAILS`
- **`offboarding`** — discovers environments for `USER_EMAILS`

Default ENVS for user create/delete when unspecified: **`dev,hx`**.

## Preconditions

1. `glab auth status` — if `invalid_grant`, tell human to run `glab auth login` on the laptop worker
2. Emails must be `@hyperexponential.com` FQDN — never invent
3. **Mutating gate** — run `glab ci run` only when one of:
   - User explicitly asked in chat, **or**
   - Slack ✅ / explicit approve on the VPN bot message (Automation), **or**
   - Continuing a recreate after a successful delete the user already approved
4. Scan/cron without approve → do **not** mutate; hand back to `jira-my-tickets` Slack approve template

## Run pipeline

```bash
glab ci run -R hyperexponential/infrastructure/tools/openvpn-automation \
  --branch main \
  -i 'ACTION:string(<action>)' \
  -i 'ENVS:array(<env1>,<env2>)' \
  -i 'USER_EMAILS:array(<email1>,<email2>)' \
  -i 'RESTART_SERVERS:bool(true)'
```

Typed inputs: `string(...)`, `array(a,b)`, `array()`, `bool(true|false)`. Always quote `-i` values with parentheses.

Capture **pipeline id** and **weburl** from output.

## Poll parent → child → jobs

Parent pipeline has generate/test + bridge `openvpn:trigger` → **child** pipeline with real work.

```bash
# Parent status
glab api "projects/74930740/pipelines/<PARENT_ID>"

# Bridge → child id
glab api "projects/74930740/pipelines/<PARENT_ID>/bridges"

# Child jobs
glab api "projects/74930740/pipelines/<CHILD_ID>/jobs?per_page=100"
```

Poll until parent + child `status` ∈ `{success, failed, canceled}`. Prefer waiting on child.

Job name patterns:

| Action | Job name example |
|--------|------------------|
| create | `openvpn:create: hx user@hyperexponential.com` |
| delete | `openvpn:delete: dev user@…` |
| restart | `openvpn:restart: hx` |

## Scrape 1Password links from create logs

After **create** child jobs succeed, for each `openvpn:create:` job:

```bash
glab api "projects/74930740/jobs/<JOB_ID>/trace"
```

Extract blocks matching (per env):

```text
Your VPN profile is ready for "<ENV>" environment.
Your username is: <EMAIL>
...
https://share.1password.com/s#...
```

Regex helpers:

- Ready line: `Your VPN profile is ready for "([^"]+)" environment`
- Username: `Your username is:\s*(\S+)`
- Share URL: `https://share\.1password\.com/s#[A-Za-z0-9_-]+`

Rules:

- **Never invent** share URLs — only paste what appears in traces
- One message (or section) per env
- Treat links as sensitive; do not commit to git or Memories
- If create succeeded but no URL found → report job URL + ask human to check logs

## Post to Slack (VPN bot)

After scrape, Send to Slack (or equivalent) roughly:

```text
VPN ready — <TICKET or email>
• hx — username <email>
  https://share.1password.com/s#...
• dev — username <email>
  https://share.1password.com/s#...
Pipelines: <parent url>
Expires ~14 days (see message in log).
```

On failure: post ticket/email, failed job name, pipeline URL, short error snippet (no secrets).

